Really, I think I think a macro could be useful here for computing a scaling factor

SENSOR_Q31_SCALER(sensitivity, shift) is half the battle. Getting the math for most sensor conversions looking like the simple integer multiplier math that it should be, could be done simpler I think in most cases. I love const table here, though sadly C doesn't let us do const math expressions like the following even if the compiler is capable to do it at compile time. Unclear if this would be done at compile or runtime.

```c
const sensitivity = SENSITIVITIES[drv_cfg->fs];
const shift = SHIFTS[drv_cfg->fs];
const int32_t scaler = (1/sensitivity)*(pow(2,31)/pow(2,shift));
q31_t scaled = sample*scaler;
```

There's also occasionally the unit conversion involved like converting G to m/s^2 would involve another multiplier of 9.81 m/s^2. But clearly it was wrong here and needed to be rectified.
